    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.06-01",
      "block_type": "definition",
      "heading": "Comparing HEP, coal, nuclear and solar",
      "text": "Energy sources should be compared against a stated service and criterion. A system may need dependable evening electricity, affordable new supply, reduced emissions or local access. The preferred option can differ with that aim and the available resources. Compare usable output, timing, fuel and operating costs, construction needs, environmental effects and system connections rather than selecting one label as best in every setting.",
