      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.06-02",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Hydroelectric power avoids fuel combustion during generation and uses a renewable water flow. Where a suitable scheme has usable storage, generation can sometimes be adjusted to demand within its limits. Construction can require substantial investment and can alter land, rivers and habitats. Output depends on flow and operating conditions; drought can constrain it. A run-of-river station should not be credited with large seasonal storage unless the actual design provides it.",
      "claim_ids": [
