    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.06-04",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Nuclear generation uses energy released through fission rather than burning a fossil fuel. Heat supports a generating process, usually involving steam and a turbine. Nuclear can supply substantial output with low direct carbon dioxide emissions during operation compared with fossil combustion. It still requires fuel, complex infrastructure, skilled operation, cooling arrangements and strong safety systems. Uranium is non-renewable and radioactive materials require appropriate management.",
