    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.06-06",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Solar photovoltaic generation avoids combustion at the point of generation and can be built at different scales. It needs no fuel, has low running costs and suits sunny places and homes far from the grid. Its disadvantages are a high cost to buy panels and batteries, and small home systems that can run lights and phones but not cooking or large appliances. Its direct output varies with sunlight and is unavailable from new sunlight during night. Storage or another source is needed if the service requires supply beyond that pattern. Manufacturing, land, materials and eventual equipment disposal also belong in a wider environmental assessment.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.4.06-1",
        "CL-6137-2.4.06-2",
