    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.06-07",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Construction cost and operating cost differ. A project with higher initial investment may have lower recurring fuel purchases, while a cheaper generator may require expensive fuel throughout operation. The comparison needs the same service, period and relevant costs. A single equipment price is not a complete lifetime cost. It also does not establish whether households can afford a tariff or an appliance needed to use the energy.",
