    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.06-08",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A hypothetical evening-service comparison makes the timing issue clear. Demand is ten energy units after sunset. A solar-only system without storage or another connection supplies no new solar generation then, even if it produced fifteen units earlier. With suitable storage, some earlier energy could be shifted, subject to capacity and losses. The daytime total alone cannot establish that the evening need is met.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.4.06-1",
        "CL-6137-2.4.06-2",
        "CL-6137-2.4.06-01-1",
