    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.06-09",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Storage calculations should state losses. Suppose ten units enter a store and eight can later be delivered under the stated efficiency. It can meet an eight-unit later load if timing and power capacity also fit, but not a ten-unit load from that charge alone. Storage is useful without being loss-free. Compare the delivered service rather than adding generated energy and stored energy as if they were two independent supplies.",
