    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.06-10",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The environmental boundary also matters. Hydropower and solar may have low operational combustion emissions while construction affects materials, habitats and land. Coal's fuel use and emissions continue during operation. Nuclear's low direct carbon dioxide emissions do not resolve waste or safety requirements. A supported evaluation identifies the relevant benefit and cost, rather than using a single adjective such as clean to stand for all environmental measures.",
      "claim_ids": [
