    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.06-11",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Supply reliability concerns the whole chain. A fuel-based plant can be unavailable during fuel disruption or maintenance; renewable output can vary with its resource; transmission can interrupt any source. Diversity, appropriate reserves, storage, maintenance and demand management can reduce different risks. The existence of more than one source is helpful only where their available output and connections cover the relevant service when needed.",
