    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.06-12",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Ruacana illustrates why a named case needs its actual design. As a run-of-river station, it uses a river resource but remains sensitive to flow. It supports a renewable contribution without proving constant annual output. A proposed solar addition could diversify daytime supply, but evening adequacy still needs a full demand and supply account. The case encourages system reasoning rather than an unsupported claim that one project makes Namibia independent of every import.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.4.06-1",
