    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.06-16",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Environmental and social costs may occur before electricity is delivered. Land acquisition, construction traffic or altered river access can affect people during development. Later benefits may not go to the same households bearing those costs. A comparison of generation options therefore needs stakeholder and timing information where the question concerns development. Compensation or participation arrangements should be assessed through their terms and delivery, not assumed from the promise of electricity.",
      "claim_ids": [
