    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.06-18",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A lower-emissions claim should identify its boundary and comparison. Avoiding combustion at a solar panel is a point-of-generation statement. Comparing construction, fuel supply, operation and disposal is a wider assessment. Neither should be substituted silently for the other. An evaluation can recognise a specific emissions benefit while still discussing land, materials, waste or safety responsibilities.",
      "claim_ids": [
